// Prologue, in medias res (SPEC §3.5 v1.1; decisions_log N-20, N-21). The party keeps its vigils
// apart in the drowned plaza of a dead city at dusk; Rhen's older voice says the one line, then the
// story cuts back to the beach where it begins (M2-FP-03 hands off to ch02/haluna at Beach).
// Grade intent: color script `prologue_iskarra_dusk` (no grade cue exists for it yet).
// Shot: P01 is a fixed wide on the plaza, the towers behind, the sun low on the left.
// The line is the human-approved text (ADR 0020 §(g)); never reword it here.
title: prologue_dead_city
location: prologue
---
@letterbox on
@camera P01
@fade in 3.0
@wait 2.0
Narrator(rhen) [tender]: Everyone I'm going to tell you about is still here tonight. Remember that, later. #line:prologue_dead_city_001 #vo
@wait 4.0
@fade out 2.5
@letterbox off
===
